= Paul Broca
{parent=List of neuroanatomists}
{c}
{wiki}
{title2=1824–1880}

A <neuroanatomist> whose historical observations helped associate left frontal injury with impaired articulate <speech>. Their interpretation is reassessed by modern lesion imaging.<Paul Broca's historic cases by Nina F. Dronkers and others>[2007, historical cases and lesion extent]{ref}

\Image[https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/file/Paul_Broca.jpg?width=260]
{width=260}
{title=Portrait of <Paul Broca>}
{source=https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paul_Broca.jpg}
{description=Pierre Petit; Wellcome Library. Public-domain photograph, via Wikimedia Commons.}

