{parent=Paul Broca}
{c}

= Santiago Ramón y Cajal
{c}
{parent=List of neuroanatomists}
{title2=1852–1934}
{wiki}

His drawings of <neurons> made their branching structure visible with extraordinary clarity. The historical illustration under <Purkinje cell> shows how different <neurons> can occupy the same part of the <cerebellum> while having strikingly different shapes.

\Image[https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/file/Cajal-Restored_crop.jpg?width=260]
{width=260}
{title=Portrait of <Santiago Ramón y Cajal>, 1899}
{source=https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cajal-Restored_crop.jpg}
{description=Anonymous photograph published by Clark University in 1899; cropped and digitally restored by Garrondo. Public-domain source, via Wikimedia Commons.}

